Z||000000||mrfixit58||11-08-2001||04:46 PM||||Does anyone know if the push-button AM/FM/ Cassette radio was an option in 88? I was looking in an 88 Owner's Manual and couldn't find it. You know the one... it had buttons instead of knobs for volume, balance, fade, and tuner.<P>------------------<BR>Roy  :D <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR>Suncoast Fieros<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG">        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Monkeyman||11-08-2001||05:20 PM||||I'm not positive, but I'm pretty sure it was a pre-'88 radio.  According to Paul Vargas (NIFE) it was the top of the line stereo from '85-'87.  He lists a different top of the line stereo for '88.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||11-08-2001||05:36 PM||||The multi buttoned push butto radio was discontinued after 87. I have one in my 87 and it is a PITA to use while driving.  Way too many buttons.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||11-08-2001||08:52 PM||||I believe that they were not available in 88.<BR>I used to have one in my Firebird. I didn't think it was too terribly difficult to use. I think they may have discontinued them due to reliability issues. The button panels used to get flaky. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfixit58||11-08-2001||09:53 PM||||Thanks guys, that's what I thought. <P>Lar, I had one in my 85 and I agree with you.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Roy<BR>||||reg||1
